{"full":"hf:M2LInES/samudra2","spaceId":"M2LInES/samudra2","name":"Samudra 2","source":"huggingface","description":"Roll a neural ocean emulator forward against GFDL-OM4","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","ocean","climate","emulation","weather","mcp-server","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-08-20T16:22:55.000Z","updated":"2026-08-20T17:38:44.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://m2lines-samudra2.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/M2LInES/samudra2","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T20:59:06.970Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T20:59:06.970Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T20:59:06.970Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🌊","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Interactive rollouts of M2LInES/Samudra2, an autoregressive neural emulator of the global ocean.","The 1° checkpoint is a ConvNeXt U-Net (84 M parameters) that maps the ocean state at two consecutive 5-day snapshots — potential temperature, salinity, zonal/meridional velocity over 19 depth levels, plus sea-surface height (77 fields → 154 channels) — together with surface forcing (wind stress, heat flux and its day-of-year anomaly) to the next two 5-day snapshots. One model step therefore advances the ocean by 10 days, and steps are chained autoregressively."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/M2LInES/samudra2/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9fe16973d7b1f39533884492aa43f1de41a3609f669a5ed3107b64296cc5294c","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:30.601Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T20:59:07.002Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Interactive rollouts of M2LInES/Samudra2, an autoregressive neural emulator of the global ocean.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/M2LInES/samudra2/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9fe16973d7b1f39533884492aa43f1de41a3609f669a5ed3107b64296cc5294